{"id":"mahabharata-6-082","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":82,"title":"द्व्यशीतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 82 · Seventh day: the night battle ends","summary":{"en":"Chitrasena is rescued and Bhishma presses Yudhishthira until the Pandava kings rally to protect him. As darkness falls the exhausted armies cease and the field becomes dreadful with jackals and spirits.","kn":"ಚಿತ್ರಸೇನನನ್ನು ರಕ್ಷಿಸಲಾಗುತ್ತದೆ; ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನನ್ನು ಒತ್ತಿದಾಗ ಪಾಂಡವ ರಾಜರು ರಕ್ಷಿಸಲು ಒಟ್ಟಾಗುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಕತ್ತಲಾದಾಗ ದಣಿದ ಸೈನ್ಯಗಳು ನಿಲ್ಲುತ್ತವೆ; ರಣರಂಗ ನರಿ, ಭೂತಗಳಿಂದ ಭಯಂಕರವಾಗುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"चित्रसेन बचाया जाता है और भीष्म युधिष्ठिर को दबाते हैं, तब पाण्डव राजा उनकी रक्षा के लिए इकट्ठे होते हैं। अँधेरा होने पर थकी सेनाएँ रुकती हैं और रणभूमि सियारों और भूतों से भयानक हो जाती है।","te":"చిత్రసేనుని రక్షిస్తారు; భీష్ముడు యుధిష్ఠిరుని ఒత్తిడి చేయగా పాండవ రాజులు అతన్ని కాపాడటానికి చేరతారు. చీకటి పడగా అలసిన సేనలు ఆగుతాయి; రణభూమి నక్కలు, భూతాలతో భయంకరమవుతుంది.","ta":"சித்ரசேனன் காக்கப்படுகிறான்; பீஷ்மர் யுதிஷ்டிரரை நெருக்க, பாண்டவ மன்னர்கள் அவரைக் காக்கத் திரள்கின்றனர். இருள் சூழ, களைத்த படைகள் நிற்கின்றன; களம் நரிகளாலும் பேய்களாலும் அச்சமூட்டுகிறது.","ml":"ചിത്രസേനൻ രക്ഷപ്പെടുന്നു; യുധിഷ്ഠിരനെ ഭീഷ്മർ സമ്മർദത്തിലാക്കുന്നു, പാണ്ഡവ രാജാക്കന്മാർ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ സംരക്ഷിക്കാൻ അണിനിരക്കുന്നു. ഇരുട്ട് വീഴുമ്പോൾ തളർന്ന സേനകൾ നിലയ്ക്കുന്നു; കുറുനരികളും ഭൂതങ്ങളും നിറഞ്ഞ് രണഭൂമി ഭയാനകമാകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.82; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"विरथं तं समासाद्य चित्रसेनं मनस्विनम् ।\nरथमारोपयामास विकर्णस्तनयस्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son Vikarna came up to the noble Chitrasena, who was without a chariot, and lifted him onto his own chariot."}},{"n":2,"text":"तस्मिंस्तथा वर्तमाने तुमुले संकुले भृशम् ।\nभीष्मः शांतनवस्तूर्णं युधिष्ठिरमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While that great and crowded turmoil went on, Bhishma, son of Shantanu, quickly rushed at Yudhishthira."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततः सरथनागाश्वाः समकम्पन्त सृञ्जयाः ।\nमृत्योरास्यमनुप्राप्तं मेनिरे च युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Srinjayas with their chariots, elephants and horses shook, and thought Yudhishthira had come into the mouth of Death."}},{"n":4,"text":"युधिष्ठिरोऽपि कौरव्यो यमाभ्यां सहितः प्रभुः ।\nमहेष्वासं नरव्याघ्रं भीष्मं शांतनवं ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira too, the Kaurava lord, with the twins, went toward Bhishma, son of Shantanu, that great bowman, tiger among men."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततः शरसहस्राणि प्रमुञ्चन्पाण्डवो युधि ।\nभीष्मं संछादयामास यथा मेघो दिवाकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Pandava, loosing thousands of arrows in the battle, covered Bhishma as a cloud covers the sun."}},{"n":6,"text":"तेन सम्यक्प्रणीतानि शरजालानि भारत ।\nप्रतिजग्राह गाङ्गेयः शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Ganga, O Bharata, caught those nets of arrows that he shot so skillfully, by hundreds and by thousands."}},{"n":7,"text":"तथैव शरजालानि भीष्मेणास्तानि मारिष ।\nआकाशे समदृश्यन्त खगमानां व्रजा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The nets of arrows that Bhishma shot were seen in the sky like flocks of birds, O revered one."}},{"n":8,"text":"निमेषार्धाच्च कौन्तेयं भीष्मः शांतनवो युधि ।\nअदृश्यं समरे चक्रे शरजालेन भागशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In half an instant Bhishma, son of Shantanu, hid the son of Kunti in the battle, piece by piece, behind a net of arrows."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा कौरव्यस्य महात्मनः ।\nनाराचं प्रेषयामास क्रुद्ध आशीविषोपमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira in anger sent an arrow like a venomous snake at the great-souled Kaurava."}},{"n":10,"text":"असंप्राप्तं ततस्तं तु क्षुरप्रेण महारथः ।\nचिच्छेद समरे राजन्भीष्मस्तस्य धनुश्च्युतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before it reached him, the great chariot-warrior Bhishma cut it down in the battle, O king, with a razor-headed arrow, as it flew from the bow."}},{"n":11,"text":"तं तु छित्त्वा रणे भीष्मो नाराचं कालसंमितम् ।\nनिजघ्ने कौरवेन्द्रस्य हयान्काञ्चनभूषणान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having cut it, Bhishma then struck down the gold-adorned horses of the Kaurava lord with an arrow like Time itself."}},{"n":12,"text":"हताश्वं तु रथं त्यक्त्वा धर्मपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nआरुरोह रथं तूर्णं नकुलस्य महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaving his horseless chariot, Yudhishthira, son of Dharma, quickly climbed onto the chariot of the great-souled Nakula."}},{"n":13,"text":"यमावपि सुसंक्रुद्धः समासाद्य रणे तदा ।\nशरैः संछादयामास भीष्मः परपुरंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, conqueror of enemy cities, enraged, then reached the twins in the battle and covered them with arrows."}},{"n":14,"text":"तौ तु दृष्ट्वा महाराज भीष्मबाणप्रपीडितौ ।\nजगामाथ परां चिन्तां भीष्मस्य वधकाङ्क्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing those two hard pressed by Bhishma's arrows, O great king, Yudhishthira fell into deep worry, desiring Bhishma's death."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो वश्यान्राज्ञस्तान्समचोदयत् ।\nभीष्मं शांतनवं सर्वे निहतेति सुहृद्गणान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira urged the kings who were under his command, and all his friends, to kill Bhishma, son of Shantanu."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततस्ते पार्थिवाः सर्वे श्रुत्वा पार्थस्य भाषितम् ।\nमहता रथवंशेन परिवव्रुः पितामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the words of Partha's brother, all those kings surrounded the grandfather with a great force of chariots."}},{"n":17,"text":"स समन्तात्परिवृतः पिता देवव्रतस्तव ।\nचिक्रीड धनुषा राजन्पातयानो महारथान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded on all sides, your father Devavrata played with his bow, O king, bringing down great chariot-warriors."}},{"n":18,"text":"तं चरन्तं रणे पार्था ददृशुः कौरवं युधि ।\nमृगमध्यं प्रविश्येव यथा सिंहशिशुं वने ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas saw that Kaurava ranging in the battle like a lion cub entering a herd of deer in the forest."}},{"n":19,"text":"तर्जयानं रणे शूरांस्त्रासयानं च सायकैः ।\nदृष्ट्वा त्रेसुर्महाराज सिंहं मृगगणा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him threatening the warriors in the battle and terrifying them with arrows, they were afraid, great king, like herds of deer before a lion."}},{"n":20,"text":"रणे भरतसिंहस्य ददृशुः क्षत्रिया गतिम् ।\nअग्नेर्वायुसहायस्य यथा कक्षं दिधक्षतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the battle the kshatriyas saw the course of that lion of the Bharatas, like fire with the wind as its helper wanting to burn dry grass."}},{"n":21,"text":"शिरांसि रथिनां भीष्मः पातयामास संयुगे ।\nतालेभ्य इव पक्वानि फलानि कुशलो नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma brought down the heads of charioteers in the battle as a skilled man brings down ripe fruit from palm trees."}},{"n":22,"text":"पतद्भिश्च महाराज शिरोभिर्धरणीतले ।\nबभूव तुमुलः शब्दः पततामश्मनामिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the heads fell to the ground, O great king, a great din arose as of stones falling."}},{"n":23,"text":"तस्मिंस्तु तुमुले युद्धे वर्तमाने सुदारुणे ।\nसर्वेषामेव सैन्यानामासीद्व्यतिकरो महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that terrible and tumultuous battle went on, there was great disorder among all the armies."}},{"n":24,"text":"भिन्नेषु तेषु व्यूहेषु क्षत्रिया इतरेतरम् ।\nएकमेकं समाहूय युद्धायैवोपतस्थिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"When those formations were broken, the kshatriyas challenged one another and stood ready to fight, man against man."}},{"n":25,"text":"शिखण्डी तु समासाद्य भरतानां पितामहम् ।\nअभिदुद्राव वेगेन तिष्ठ तिष्ठेति चाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Shikhandi, reaching the grandfather of the Bharatas, rushed at him with speed and said, \"Stand, stand!\""}},{"n":26,"text":"अनादृत्य ततो भीष्मस्तं शिखण्डिनमाहवे ।\nप्रययौ सृञ्जयान्क्रुद्धः स्त्रीत्वं चिन्त्य शिखण्डिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Bhishma, taking no notice of Shikhandi in the battle, remembering that he had been a woman, went angrily against the Srinjayas."}},{"n":27,"text":"सृञ्जयास्तु ततो हृष्टा दृष्ट्वा भीष्मं महारथम् ।\nसिंहनादान्बहुविधांश्चक्रुः शङ्खविमिश्रितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Srinjayas, delighted to see that great chariot-warrior Bhishma come, raised many kinds of lion roars mixed with the sound of conches."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततः प्रववृते युद्धं व्यतिषक्तरथद्विपम् ।\nअपरां दिशमास्थाय स्थिते सवितरि प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the battle began again, with chariots and elephants entangled, as the sun, O lord, stood in the western quarter."}},{"n":29,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नोऽथ पाञ्चाल्यः सात्यकिश्च महारथः ।\nपीडयन्तौ भृशं सैन्यं शक्तितोमरवृष्टिभिः ।\nशस्त्रैश्च बहुभी राजञ्जघ्नतुस्तावकान्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna, the Panchala, and the great chariot-warrior Satyaki, pressing the army hard with showers of spears and lances and with many weapons, struck down your men in the battle."}},{"n":30,"text":"ते हन्यमानाः समरे तावकाः पुरुषर्षभ ।\nआर्यां युद्धे मतिं कृत्वा न त्यजन्ति स्म संयुगम् ।\nयथोत्साहं च समरे जघ्नुर्लोकं महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Being slaughtered in the battle, your men, O bull among men, held to the noble resolve in fighting and did not leave the field; those great chariot-warriors killed people with all the zeal they had."}},{"n":31,"text":"तत्राक्रन्दो महानासीत्तावकानां महात्मनाम् ।\nवध्यतां समरे राजन्पार्षतेन महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great wail rose among your great-souled men as they were slain in the battle by the great-souled son of Prishata, O king."}},{"n":32,"text":"तं श्रुत्वा निनदं घोरं तावकानां महारथौ ।\nविन्दानुविन्दावावन्त्यौ पार्षतं प्रत्युपस्थितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that terrible cry of your men, the two great chariot-warriors, the Avanti brothers Vinda and Anuvinda, came against the son of Prishata."}},{"n":33,"text":"तौ तस्य तुरगान्हत्वा त्वरमाणौ महारथौ ।\nछादयामासतुरुभौ शरवर्षेण पार्षतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two great chariot-warriors, hurrying, killed his horses and covered Prishata's son with a rain of arrows."}},{"n":34,"text":"अवप्लुत्याथ पाञ्चाल्यो रथात्तूर्णं महाबलः ।\nआरुरोह रथं तूर्णं सात्यकेः सुमहात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty Panchala leapt quickly from his chariot and quickly mounted the chariot of the great-souled Satyaki."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा महत्या सेनया वृतः ।\nआवन्त्यौ समरे क्रुद्धावभ्ययात्स परंतपौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira, surrounded by a great army, advanced on the two enraged Avantis, tormentors of foes."}},{"n":36,"text":"तथैव तव पुत्रोऽपि सर्वोद्योगेन मारिष ।\nविन्दानुविन्दावावन्त्यौ परिवार्योपतस्थिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son too, O revered one, with all his effort, surrounded the Avanti brothers Vinda and Anuvinda and came to their aid."}},{"n":37,"text":"अर्जुनश्चापि संक्रुद्धः क्षत्रियान्क्षत्रियर्षभ ।\nअयोधयत संग्रामे वज्रपाणिरिवासुरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna too, enraged, fought the kshatriyas in the battle, O bull among kshatriyas, like the thunderbolt-wielder fighting asuras."}},{"n":38,"text":"द्रोणश्च समरे क्रुद्धः पुत्रस्य प्रियकृत्तव ।\nव्यधमत्सर्वपाञ्चालांस्तूलराशिमिवानलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Drona, enraged in the battle, doing what pleased your son, destroyed all the Panchalas as fire destroys a heap of cotton."}},{"n":39,"text":"दुर्योधनपुरोगास्तु पुत्रास्तव विशां पते ।\nपरिवार्य रणे भीष्मं युयुधुः पाण्डवैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your sons, led by Duryodhana, surrounded Bhishma in the battle and fought the Pandavas."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनो राजा लोहितायति भास्करे ।\nअब्रवीत्तावकान्सर्वांस्त्वरध्वमिति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, as the sun was reddening, King Duryodhana said to all your men, O Bharata, \"Hurry!\""}},{"n":41,"text":"युध्यतां तु तथा तेषां कुर्वतां कर्म दुष्करम् ।\nअस्तं गिरिमथारूढे नप्रकाशति भास्करे ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they fought, performing hard deeds, the sun climbed the setting mountain and stopped shining."}},{"n":42,"text":"प्रावर्तत नदी घोरा शोणितौघतरङ्गिणी ।\nगोमायुगणसंकीर्णा क्षणेन रजनीमुखे ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the edge of night, in a moment a terrible river arose, its waves floods of blood, crowded with packs of jackals."}},{"n":43,"text":"शिवाभिरशिवाभिश्च रुवद्भिर्भैरवं रवम् ।\nघोरमायोधनं जज्ञे भूतसंघसमाकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With jackals howling, both auspicious and ill-omened, a fearful roar went up and the battlefield became horrible, thronged with crowds of spirits."}},{"n":44,"text":"राक्षसाश्च पिशाचाश्च तथान्ये पिशिताशनाः ।\nसमन्ततो व्यदृश्यन्त शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rakshasas, pishachas and other flesh-eaters were seen on every side, in hundreds and thousands."}},{"n":45,"text":"अर्जुनोऽथ सुशर्मादीन्राज्ञस्तान्सपदानुगान् ।\nविजित्य पृतनामध्ये ययौ स्वशिबिरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna, having beaten Susharman and the other kings with their followers in the midst of the army, went toward his own camp."}},{"n":46,"text":"युधिष्ठिरोऽपि कौरव्यो भ्रातृभ्यां सहितस्तदा ।\nययौ स्वशिबिरं राजा निशायां सेनया वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira too, the Kaurava, then went with his two brothers, surrounded by his army, to his own camp in the night."}},{"n":47,"text":"भीमसेनोऽपि राजेन्द्र दुर्योधनमुखान्रथान् ।\nअवजित्य ततः संख्ये ययौ स्वशिबिरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena too, O king of kings, having beaten Duryodhana and the chariot-warriors led by him in the battle, went to his own camp."}},{"n":48,"text":"दुर्योधनोऽपि नृपतिः परिवार्य महारणे ।\nभीष्मं शांतनवं तूर्णं प्रयातः शिबिरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Duryodhana too, surrounding Bhishma, son of Shantanu, in the great battle, quickly went to his camp."}},{"n":49,"text":"द्रोणो द्रौणिः कृपः शल्यः कृतवर्मा च सात्वतः ।\nपरिवार्य चमूं सर्वां प्रययुः शिबिरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona, Ashvatthama, Kripa, Shalya and Kritavarman the Satvata surrounded the whole army and went to the camp."}},{"n":50,"text":"तथैव सात्यकी राजन्धृष्टद्युम्नश्च पार्षतः ।\nपरिवार्य रणे योधान्ययतुः शिबिरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too Satyaki and Dhrishtadyumna, son of Prishata, surrounded the warriors in the battle and went to the camp."}},{"n":51,"text":"एवमेते महाराज तावकाः पाण्डवैः सह ।\nपर्यवर्तन्त सहिता निशाकाले परंतपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this way your men and the Pandavas, tormentors of foes, all went back together at nightfall."}},{"n":52,"text":"ततः स्वशिबिरं गत्वा पाण्डवाः कुरवस्तथा ।\nन्यविशन्त महाराज पूजयन्तः परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having gone to their own camps, the Pandavas and the Kurus settled down, honoring one another, O great king."}},{"n":53,"text":"रक्षां कृत्वात्मनः शूरा न्यस्य गुल्मान्यथाविधि ।\nअपनीय च शल्यांस्ते स्नात्वा च विविधैर्जलैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The heroes set guards for themselves and posted their companies in due order, drew out their arrows, and bathed in waters of many kinds."}},{"n":54,"text":"कृतस्वस्त्ययनाः सर्वे संस्तूयन्तश्च बन्दिभिः ।\nगीतवादित्रशब्देन व्यक्रीडन्त यशस्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All, having performed rites of blessing and being praised by bards, those glorious men amused themselves with song and the sound of instruments."}},{"n":55,"text":"मुहूर्तमिव तत्सर्वमभवत्स्वर्गसंनिभम् ।\nन हि युद्धकथां कांचित्तत्र चक्रुर्महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a moment it was all like heaven. The great chariot-warriors did not speak any talk of war there."}},{"n":56,"text":"ते प्रसुप्ते बले तत्र परिश्रान्तजने नृप ।\nहस्त्यश्वबहुले राजन्प्रेक्षणीये बभूवतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When their weary people slept, O king, the camps full of elephants and horses were a sight to see."}}]}]}